     Sum of `primes[idx+1 : idx+1+num_after]` is `prefix_sum[idx+1+num_after] - prefix_sum[idx+1]`.
   - Let `f(idx) = primes[idx] + prefix_sum[idx+1+num_after] - prefix_sum[idx+1]`.
   - Binary search for the largest `idx` in `[min_idx, max_idx]` with `f(idx) <= remaining_sum`.
   - Append `primes[idx]` to `res`, subtract `primes[idx]` from `remaining_sum`, set `last_idx = idx`.
7. Return `res`.

